From 9799e42030f954594fa1d3f667b412d92b28bc25 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bare <git@barebrowser.org>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 17:13:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Stop advertising Safe Browsing, which has no handler in this
 build

Chromium Android reaches Safe Browsing through SafeBrowsingApiBridge, which
needs a handler injected at startup. Nothing in a public build injects one:
the only callers of setSafeBrowsingApiHandler and setSafetyNetApiHandler are
tests, and the bridge itself says so at the null check. Google supplies the
handler downstream. So every lookup short-circuits and no interstitial can
ever appear.

The settings still offered Standard and Enhanced Protection, Safety Hub
carried a module reporting protection state, Safety Check listed a row, and
the new tab page could promote Enhanced Protection. All of it described
something that does not run.

Removed the privacy row, the /safeBrowsing deep link, the three navigation
cases, the settings-search entries, the Safety Hub module, the Safety Check
row and the promo card. The Safety Check binder now tolerates the missing
row rather than dereferencing it.

Nothing about the underlying lookup path changed. It was already inert.
